In conclusion, our study applied YOLOv8n and YOLOv8s models to a
custom dataset for detecting objects on a solar panel. We deliberately chose
a non-industrial solar panel, creating realistic conditions with dry leaves,
sand, and bird droppings. Video footage, captured using an iPhone with 4K
resolution at 23.99 frames per second, was processed using OpenCV. We
annotated frames and applied YOLO models for effective object detection.
The results shows that yolov8s has an accuracy of87.5% and the yolo8n has
an accuracy of 97.1%. This shows that the yolov8n has performed better
than the yolov8s and is suitable for object detection over the surface of solar
panel.
